  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Karnail Singh And Another vs State Of U.P. on 29 July, 2020 Author: Gautam Chowdhary Bench: Gautam Chowdhary High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 52 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 19363 of 2020 Applicant :- Karnail Singh And Another Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Anand Ji Mishra,Kaushal Kumar Pandey Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Gautam Chowdhary,J. The instant bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicants, Karnail Singh and Vikram, with a prayer to release them on bail in Case Crime No. 138 of 2020, under Sections 147, 149, 272, 273, 307 Ipc and 60 Excise Act, Police Station Kithore, District- Meerut, during pendency of trial. Submission is that implication of applicants is under Section 307 Ipc.",
    "facts": "Intention of the applicant was only to evade arrest by the police and he fired only to frighten the police.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicants further submits that the incident is said to have taken place on the side of the Barsati River i.e. open public place but there is no independent witness of the alleged Karnail Singh And Another vs State Of U.P. on 29 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/76212406/ 1 recovery. False recovery has been alleged. It has been submitted that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. The applicant is languishing in jail since 07.4.2020. Learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant. Having considered the material on record, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicants involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on their furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1. The applicants shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence by intimidating/ pressurizing the witnesses, during the investigation or trial. 2. The applicants shall cooperate in the trial sincerely without seeking any adjournment. 3. The applicants shall not indulge in any criminal activity or commission of any crime after being released on bail. 4.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicants further submits that the incident is said to have taken place on the side of the Barsati River i.e. open public place but there is no independent witness of the alleged Karnail Singh And Another vs State Of U.P. on 29 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/76212406/ 1 recovery.",
    "respondent_arguments": "False recovery has been alleged. It has been submitted that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. The applicant is languishing in jail since 07.4.2020. Learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Having considered the material on record, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicants involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on their furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1. The applicants shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence by intimidating/ pressurizing the witnesses, during the investigation or trial. 2. The applicants shall cooperate in the trial sincerely without seeking any adjournment. 3. The applicants shall not indulge in any criminal activity or commission of any crime after being released on bail. 4."
